# Login UI freeze (user lock)

**Owner instruction (2026-09-07):** Stick to the **current** login UI for **all** portals. Do **not** change it in development until the user explicitly says to.

## Frozen surfaces (do not restyle / redesign)

| Route | Implementation |
|-------|----------------|
| `/auth/login` | `src/app/auth/login/page.js` |
| `/admin/login` | `src/app/admin/(auth)/login/page.jsx` |
| `/faculty/login` · `/student/login` | `src/components/auth/PortalLoginPage.jsx` |
| Forgot / reset | `src/app/auth/forgot-password/page.jsx`, `src/app/auth/reset-password/page.jsx` (same centered card family) |

## Locked pattern (preserve exactly)

- Centered Quirri card on mist canvas — **not** split-hero, **not** `new_updated_design_four/Login.dc.html`
- Poppins on auth cards; official `QuirriLogo` centered
- Copy: **Welcome back** / **Sign in to Quirri** (portal-specific subcopy only where already present)
- Catalog fields (`email`, `password`) + Amber 700 **Sign in** CTA
- Shared auth CSS / card chrome — do not invent a second login look

## Allowed without unfreezing

- Auth **logic** only: API wiring, role redirects, cookie cleanup, lockout, validation via `FIELD_RULES` / schemas
- Bug fixes that restore the **existing** look (broken layout, a11y regressions) — not a redesign

## Forbidden until user says otherwise

- Visual redesign, layout changes, new login templates, Figma/design-pack login restyles
- Adopting `Login.dc.html` or any post-login shell styling on auth screens
- “While we’re here” polish on login pages during unrelated work

**Unfreeze:** only when the user explicitly asks to change login UI.
